<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Who runs PipeMetric and what sourcing assistance actually covers — an honest list of what we can and cannot do."
  path="/about/"
>
<h1>About</h1>
<p class="lede">PipeMetric is run by <strong>Steven</strong>, the project owner — not a team, not a factory, not a marketplace.</p>

<h2>What this site is</h2>
<p>A free steel pipe weight calculator with documented dimension data (ASME B36.10-2022 / B36.19-2022), plus plain-language guides for specifying and sourcing pipe. The calculator runs entirely in your browser — your inputs never leave your device.</p>

<h2>Sourcing assistance — what we can do</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Help interpret and organize your pipe specification (including Chinese–English conversion)</li>
  <li>Complete a rough requirement into a quotable RFQ</li>
  <li>Look for potential supply channels in China and make initial contact</li>
  <li>Screen suppliers and help collect and relay quotations</li>
</ul>
<p>Typical first response time: <strong>within 2 business days</strong>.</p>

<h2>What we cannot do (yet)</h2>
<ul>
  <li>No own stock, no factory operation</li>
  <li>No committed pricing, lead times, financing, or guarantees</li>
  <li>No QC / inspection, logistics / customs clearance, or after-sales handling</li>
  <li>No performance or fulfillment warranties</li>
</ul>
<p>Quotations from third parties are always labeled <em>Quote provided by third-party supplier</em>. If we cannot source an item, we say so explicitly and close the inquiry — we do not leave requests hanging.</p>
</Layout>
